WEBVTT

00:03:57.817 --> 00:04:00.528
but we don't get to go around
believing whatever we like."

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.281
George Bernard Shaw tells us

00:04:03.322 --> 00:04:06.909
that the power of accurate observation
is commonly called "cynicism"

00:04:06.951 --> 00:04:08.661
by those who haven't got it.

00:04:08.703 --> 00:04:10.788
(Laughter)

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.248
107 years later,

00:04:12.248 --> 00:04:14.667
the cartoon philosopher Lisa Simpson

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:18.296
taught us that as intelligence goes up,
happiness goes down.

00:04:19.463 --> 00:04:20.881
Maybe hope does, too.

00:04:21.382 --> 00:04:24.010
Maybe cynicism
is the price of being right.

00:04:25.136 --> 00:04:26.721
Most people think so.

00:04:26.762 --> 00:04:29.640
70 percent think cynics
are smarter than noncynics;

00:04:29.682 --> 00:04:32.393
85 percent think they would make
better lie detectors.